1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,480
At cold dawn, toxic smog chokes Delhi schoolchildren.

2
00:00:05,480 --> 00:00:09,720
Inversions trap the smoke and outdated warnings arrive too late.

3
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:14,880
We built AERIS, an atmospheric early-warning platform tracking what is in the air, warning

4
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:19,120
those most exposed, and changing what happens on bad days.

5
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:26,200
Here, we resolve the airshed down to high-resolution 3-km grid cells across 33 ground monitoring stations.

6
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:32,000
AERIS continuously ingests all 33 ground stations in real time, plotting network-wide pollutant

7
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:35,080
profiles against national air standards.

8
00:00:35,080 --> 00:00:40,760
In Tab 2, the Citizen Portal, AERIS empowers administrators with our CAQM engine, generating

9
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:46,480
statutory enforcement orders under the CAQM Act 2021 in a single click.

10
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:51,200
Scanning the QR code allows instant mobile onboarding on the local network.

11
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:56,240
A citizen enters their email and our multi-agent engine dispatches a verified emergency

12
00:00:56,240 --> 00:01:00,280
air warning to their inbox via real-time SMTP.

13
00:01:00,280 --> 00:01:05,840
For schools, AERIS issues dynamic GRAP-IV directives, suspending morning outdoor assemblies

14
00:01:05,840 --> 00:01:09,200
and pinpointing safe indoor ventilation windows.

15
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:15,720
In Tab 3, AERIS predicts air quality 72 hours in advance using Koopman dynamical rollouts.

16
00:01:15,720 --> 00:01:25,000
Watch as we toggle between AQI, PM2.5, PM10, Ozone, and Nitrogen Dioxide with analytical Lyapunov uncertainty bounds.

17
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,920
In Tab 4, we model the critical thermal inversion lid.

18
00:01:28,920 --> 00:01:35,200
As nocturnal radiative cooling collapses the boundary layer to under 200 meters, PM2.5 particulates

19
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:39,600
are violently trapped near ground level during early morning hours.

20
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:45,560
In Tab 5, we ingest live satellite fire radiative power from NASA FIRMS to track active stubble fires,

21
00:01:45,560 --> 00:01:52,320
projecting smoke advection into Delhi using our Plume Clock trajectory integrator and regional advection timeline.

22
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:57,040
Instead of passive monitoring, AERIS changes what happens on bad days.

23
00:01:57,040 --> 00:02:01,600
Our Sequential Least Squares Model Predictive Control algorithm computes optimal municipal

24
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:06,560
intervention schedules, cutting peak PM2.5 by up to 32%.

25
00:02:06,560 --> 00:02:11,960
Crucially, AERIS models Airshed Federalism through economic arbitrage, showing that funding upwind

26
00:02:11,960 --> 00:02:17,480
biomass remediation in Punjab yields 6.9 times higher clean air return per rupee than

27
00:02:17,480 --> 00:02:21,040
intra-Delhi lockdowns, resolving the Nash deadlock.

28
00:02:21,040 --> 00:02:27,120
In Tab 7, all 33 stations stream live sensor diagnostics, cross-pollutant ratios, and spatial

29
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:30,360
Pearson cross-correlations across Delhi wards.

30
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:36,760
AERIS is architected to run entirely on open-source AWS tooling locally with zero cloud cost.

31
00:02:36,760 --> 00:02:42,280
We use AWS Cedar for policy authorization, OpenSearch for geospatial indexing, and

32
00:02:42,280 --> 00:02:45,320
Strands Agents SDK for multi-agent reasoning.

33
00:02:45,320 --> 00:02:50,520
In Tab 9, our model achieves a proven RMSE of 14.8 micrograms per cubic meter.

34
00:02:50,520 --> 00:02:57,200
All validation weights, benchmarks, and reproducible datasets are verified in our public Google Drive proof repository.

35
00:02:57,200 --> 00:03:04,920
AERIS empowers citizens, schools, and city administrators to take control of their air and breathe easier.

36
00:03:04,920 --> 00:03:05,440
Thank you.
